-- title:
--   Typed primitives modulo Pi span at most a line
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $j_0 \colon \mathbb{Z}_{q^2} \to k$ be a ring homomorphism, where $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ denotes `Zp2 q`, the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements. Let $X_0$ be a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $k$ relative to $j_0$: a commutative two-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $k$ together with an action $a \mapsto [a]$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ and an endomorphism $\Pi =$ `X₀.varpi` by law homomorphisms, satisfying $[1] = \mathrm{id}$, $[ab] = [a]\circ[b]$, $[a+b] = [a] +_F [b]$, $\Pi\circ\Pi = [q]$ and $\Pi\circ[a] = [\sigma(a)]\circ\Pi$ for the Frobenius $\sigma$, whose tangent space splits as the direct sum of the complementary invertible submodules `lieZero j₀` and `lieOne j₀` and which has height $4$ in the sense that $[q]$ has kernel of degree $q^4$. Let $\psi \colon \mathbb{Z}_{q^2} \to k$ be an arbitrary function and let $g, g'$ be power series in two variables over $k$ with zero constant term such that: the additive coboundary $\partial_F g = g(F(X,Y)) - g(X) - g(Y)$, and likewise $\partial_F g'$, lies in the ideal of $k[[X_0,X_1,Y_0,Y_1]]$ generated by the two components of $\Pi$ evaluated at the $X$-variables together with the two components of $\Pi$ evaluated at the $Y$-variables; and for every $a \in \mathbb{Z}_{q^2}$ both $g\circ[a] - \psi(a)\,g$ and $g'\circ[a] - \psi(a)\,g'$ lie in the ideal $(\Pi_0,\Pi_1)$ of $k[[X_0,X_1]]$. Then there are $c, c' \in k$, not both zero, with $c\,g + c'\,g' \in (\Pi_0,\Pi_1)$.
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation this says that, for a special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of height $4$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, the primitives modulo $\Pi$ of a fixed $\psi$-type form a space of dimension at most one modulo the ideal generated by $\Pi$. It is used in the computation of the lines of typed primitives modulo the iterated $\Pi$-series, where the corresponding space is shown to have rank two.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalODModule_exists_smul_add_smul_mem_span_varpi_of_addCoboundary_mem.lean

